1	// Acceptance tests for the change request:
2	//   "Let me record what a client has paid on an invoice. Store the amount and the date. Show it on
3	//    the invoice."
4	//
5	// An invoice can now carry a record of what the client has PAID against it. On the invoice's own
6	// detail page (invoice-detail-page, reached by navigating to /invoices/<id> — the same public URL
7	// surface the invoice specs already use) a payments region (invoice-payments) lists every payment
8	// recorded on THAT invoice in a table (invoice-payments-table). Each payment row (payment-row-<id>)
9	// shows the two things stored for it: the AMOUNT paid (payment-amount) and the DATE it was paid
10	// (payment-date). A form (payment-form) records a new payment from those two fields
11	// (payment-form-amount / payment-form-date, submitted with payment-form-submit), refusing an
12	// incomplete one with payment-form-error.
13	//
14	// Asserts ONLY through the UI (data-testid). Data is arranged via resetAndSeed, which honours
15	// payments: { id, invoiceId, amount, date } (alongside clients / projects / invoices). This change
16	// introduces NO new audit record, so nothing is asserted through the audit channel here.
17	//
18	// The payment amount is MONEY but payment-amount is a NEW anchor, not one of the three money-format
19	// anchors the money-format spec pins exactly; so it is matched leniently (a leading "$" and a
20	// trailing ".00" both optional) — the exact presentation is not what this change pins. The date is
21	// asserted format-tolerantly the way invoice-dates does: a date rendering ("2025-06-15",
